WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.087 --> 00:00:01.611
- Knock, knock. Who's there?

00:00:01.611 --> 00:00:03.411
- (man) Who there?

00:00:03.411 --> 00:00:05.354
- Me and this *Bleeped* broccoli that

00:00:05.354 --> 00:00:06.721
I'm about to make you eat.

00:00:06.721 --> 00:00:08.256
No, that's my own.

00:00:08.256 --> 00:00:11.006
(Dramatic music)

00:00:17.998 --> 00:00:19.150
- I hate broccoli.

00:00:19.150 --> 00:00:21.105
- I hate everything about broccoli.

00:00:21.105 --> 00:00:23.272
- I hate broccoli.

00:00:23.272 --> 00:00:24.152
- My parents tried to serve me broccoli

00:00:24.152 --> 00:00:26.599
a bunch of different ways,
and at the end of the day,

00:00:26.599 --> 00:00:28.828
as soon as they left the
room, I would often just

00:00:28.828 --> 00:00:30.055
throw it away.

00:00:30.055 --> 00:00:31.845
- Whenever I go out to eat with friends

00:00:31.845 --> 00:00:34.369
and I get broccoli on my dish,

00:00:34.369 --> 00:00:36.889
I always give it away to somebody else.

00:00:36.889 --> 00:00:39.799
- I went on a date where a guy told me

00:00:39.799 --> 00:00:41.559
he was going to cook me dinner.

00:00:41.559 --> 00:00:43.319
And it was a nice steak, which I love,

00:00:43.319 --> 00:00:45.756
and then a huge side of
broccoli, which I hate.

00:00:45.756 --> 00:00:48.994
Do I eat the broccoli and
hope I don't throw up?

00:00:48.994 --> 00:00:53.474
Or do I not eat the broccoli
and then I'm the 22 year old

00:00:53.474 --> 00:00:55.528
who still won't eat her vegetables?

00:00:55.528 --> 00:00:58.022
So I ended up just pushing
it around my plate.

00:00:58.022 --> 00:00:59.918
Never saw him again. So.

00:00:59.918 --> 00:01:02.343
- I just think there
is no way that anybody

00:01:02.343 --> 00:01:03.862
could make me like broccoli.

00:01:03.862 --> 00:01:05.410
- There is nothing that any of

00:01:05.410 --> 00:01:07.364
these chefs can do to
get me to like broccoli.

00:01:07.364 --> 00:01:09.165
It's been tried. It's not going to happen.

00:01:09.165 --> 00:01:10.982
- I don't think there is anything

00:01:10.982 --> 00:01:13.982
you can do to make me like broccoli.

00:01:15.544 --> 00:01:17.734
My name is Ross Pineda, currently a

00:01:17.734 --> 00:01:19.476
junior sioux chef over at Pig and Cow.

00:01:19.476 --> 00:01:21.569
Been cooking professionally
for about three years now.

00:01:21.569 --> 00:01:23.150
- I'm happy, healthy, latina.

00:01:23.150 --> 00:01:25.781
Aka chef Yadi. Aka the vegetable slayer.

00:01:25.781 --> 00:01:29.557
And I'm bringing that plant
based natural Caribbean flavor

00:01:29.557 --> 00:01:31.032
to all the cooking that I do.

00:01:31.032 --> 00:01:33.612
I think I've been cooking
professionally for about

00:01:33.612 --> 00:01:36.244
five years. A lot of the work that I do is

00:01:36.244 --> 00:01:38.193
actually with children, and so

00:01:38.193 --> 00:01:40.989
I'm constantly having to
hide and tuck vegetables

00:01:40.989 --> 00:01:44.440
and blend them and deconstruct
it and bring it in some way.

00:01:44.440 --> 00:01:47.155
- I have to be a picky
eater. Since growing up,

00:01:47.155 --> 00:01:48.578
I've had a lot of allergies.

00:01:48.578 --> 00:01:49.648
You kind of grow around it and

00:01:49.648 --> 00:01:51.032
learn how to substitute things.

00:01:51.032 --> 00:01:52.339
With my experience with picky eaters,

00:01:52.339 --> 00:01:54.292
It's a little bit difficult
sometimes, not going to lie.

00:01:54.292 --> 00:01:55.921
At the end of the day, you got
to make everybody satisfied

00:01:55.921 --> 00:01:57.215
with what you do and what you cook.

00:01:57.215 --> 00:01:58.638
For all y'all picky eaters out there,

00:01:58.638 --> 00:02:00.029
we trying to meet y'all. Come see us.

00:02:00.029 --> 00:02:01.690
- Bring us our victims.

00:02:01.690 --> 00:02:02.538
- Throwing it down.

00:02:02.538 --> 00:02:03.931
- We're ready to make believers.

00:02:03.931 --> 00:02:05.576
- We here that you're one of these people

00:02:05.576 --> 00:02:07.467
now that don't like broccoli. Why is that?

00:02:07.467 --> 00:02:09.649
- I don't like the taste,
I don't like the smell,

00:02:09.649 --> 00:02:12.532
I don't like the texture,
I don't like the color,

00:02:12.532 --> 00:02:14.305
I don't like the gag reflex it gives me.

00:02:14.305 --> 00:02:15.478
- Oh, it makes you gag!

00:02:15.478 --> 00:02:16.774
Oh, that's a new level of hate!

00:02:16.774 --> 00:02:18.357
- Oh, that's new!

00:02:18.357 --> 00:02:20.708
- I think it's the texture, you know.

00:02:20.708 --> 00:02:22.163
- Texture.

00:02:22.163 --> 00:02:24.427
- Just, like, the little
fuzzy bits on the top of it.

00:02:24.427 --> 00:02:26.327
- Florets. We learn something new today.

00:02:26.327 --> 00:02:27.160
- [Yadi] Yes!

00:02:27.160 --> 00:02:29.763
- I don't understand how
you're supposed to eat it.

00:02:29.763 --> 00:02:31.296
It confuses me. Do I eat the top?

00:02:31.296 --> 00:02:33.743
Do I eat the bottom? Do I
eat it all at the same time?

00:02:33.743 --> 00:02:36.998
- Our taste buds change, our
pallets develop and change

00:02:36.998 --> 00:02:39.344
as we get older. I
think you have this scar

00:02:39.344 --> 00:02:41.624
with broccoli, but you may not...

00:02:41.624 --> 00:02:42.917
- Lots of scars.

00:02:42.917 --> 00:02:45.647
- You may not have... lots
of scars. Emotional scars.

00:02:45.647 --> 00:02:47.712
- I think the only times
I've ever been presented

00:02:47.712 --> 00:02:49.581
with broccoli it's just been steamed.

00:02:49.581 --> 00:02:51.220
And it's just not....

00:02:51.220 --> 00:02:53.265
- Well, this is what I'm
always talking about.

00:02:53.265 --> 00:02:54.748
It's not that people
don't like vegetables,

00:02:54.748 --> 00:02:56.013
it's that they don't do the
same things to vegetables

00:02:56.013 --> 00:02:58.933
that they do let's say to like proteins.

00:02:58.933 --> 00:03:00.332
Season it, put sauces on it.

00:03:00.332 --> 00:03:02.282
- What are the kind of
things you do like to eat?

00:03:02.282 --> 00:03:03.555
- Spicy food.

00:03:03.555 --> 00:03:04.461
- Okay.

00:03:04.461 --> 00:03:05.294
- Savory things.

00:03:05.294 --> 00:03:06.288
- Very herbaceous foods.

00:03:06.288 --> 00:03:07.752
- I like savory, like spicy.

00:03:07.752 --> 00:03:09.631
- I dance when I'm happy.

00:03:09.631 --> 00:03:10.464
- Yeah.

00:03:10.464 --> 00:03:11.410
- So you're saying things that I like,

00:03:11.410 --> 00:03:12.572
so like savory, spicy.

00:03:12.572 --> 00:03:14.824
You're going to be in a
situationship with broccoli

00:03:14.824 --> 00:03:15.888
after today, okay?

00:03:15.888 --> 00:03:16.721
- Okay, I can get with that.

00:03:16.721 --> 00:03:18.280
- Not a relationship,
just a situationship.

00:03:18.280 --> 00:03:20.346
- A one night stem, if I might add.

00:03:20.346 --> 00:03:21.179
- Good luck.

00:03:21.179 --> 00:03:22.012
- Thank you.

00:03:22.012 --> 00:03:22.845
- I appreciate it.

00:03:22.845 --> 00:03:23.678
- Y'all need it.

00:03:23.678 --> 00:03:24.511
- May the odds be ever in your favor.

00:03:24.511 --> 00:03:26.983
- I think they're going to go from hating

00:03:26.983 --> 00:03:28.589
broccoli to at least mildly liking it

00:03:28.589 --> 00:03:29.942
or possibly loving it.

00:03:29.942 --> 00:03:32.517
- Who knows what is going to happen.

00:03:32.517 --> 00:03:35.100
(Upbeat music)

00:03:36.216 --> 00:03:38.593
- [Yadi] I cannot wait to mix in

00:03:38.593 --> 00:03:41.828
Dominican and Caribbean
flavors into vegetables.

00:03:41.828 --> 00:03:44.850
I decided to go two
chains on this broccoli.

00:03:44.850 --> 00:03:47.312
I'm going to make it two
ways and I'm going to

00:03:47.312 --> 00:03:49.389
deconstruct it. First I'm
going to bring it into a

00:03:49.389 --> 00:03:51.454
broccoli, corn, and
black eyed pea fritter.

00:03:51.454 --> 00:03:53.547
And then I'm going to
do a charred broccoli

00:03:53.547 --> 00:03:55.936
chimichurri sauce on the bottom.

00:03:55.936 --> 00:03:57.499
I don't think they're expecting some heat,

00:03:57.499 --> 00:03:59.402
some spice, some savoriness.

00:03:59.402 --> 00:04:01.903
I'm bringing sweet corn into my fritters

00:04:01.903 --> 00:04:04.277
to balance out the broccoli taste.

00:04:04.277 --> 00:04:06.283
But my chimichurri has
sofrito in it which is a

00:04:06.283 --> 00:04:09.450
Dominican Caribbean green spice blend.

00:04:11.395 --> 00:04:14.447
So that's my kind of
different little take on it.

00:04:14.447 --> 00:04:16.245
- Got a little trick up my sleeve.

00:04:16.245 --> 00:04:19.417
What I'm going to be
making is a corn aioli

00:04:19.417 --> 00:04:23.329
with a chimichurri mixed inside. Shhhh!

00:04:23.329 --> 00:04:25.056
People are always like scared about the

00:04:25.056 --> 00:04:27.516
flavor of broccoli. The
char adds flavor and

00:04:27.516 --> 00:04:29.506
disguises the broccoli.

00:04:29.506 --> 00:04:30.690
If you like BBQ, you like anything

00:04:30.690 --> 00:04:32.090
charred, you know what I mean?

00:04:32.090 --> 00:04:34.335
I think that introducing the corn with

00:04:34.335 --> 00:04:37.130
the chimichurri will make it over the top.

00:04:37.130 --> 00:04:39.713
(upbeat music)

00:04:43.368 --> 00:04:45.261
- [Yadi] So much broccoli!

00:04:45.261 --> 00:04:46.416
- [Ross] Mad broccoli, right?

00:04:46.416 --> 00:04:47.813
- [Yadi] Mad broccoli, son!

00:04:47.813 --> 00:04:48.993
They said they like spice,
they like herbiness,

00:04:48.993 --> 00:04:52.384
they like brightness.
So I got Jalapeno to get

00:04:52.384 --> 00:04:54.036
Jalap in your face. I
got some chopped cilantro

00:04:54.036 --> 00:04:56.667
for the herbiness and I'm
coming back with the zester.

00:04:56.667 --> 00:05:00.469
So, we've got some
broccoli corn fritters here

00:05:00.469 --> 00:05:02.960
over a charred broccoli
sofrito chimichurri

00:05:02.960 --> 00:05:06.709
with jalapeno, fresh cilantro,
and lemon zest garnish.

00:05:06.709 --> 00:05:09.480
We came to slay the broccoli game.

00:05:09.480 --> 00:05:11.398
- [Ross] So, I finally finished my plate.

00:05:11.398 --> 00:05:13.248
What we have here is a charred

00:05:13.248 --> 00:05:16.843
broccoli charred corn aioli with sirloin

00:05:16.843 --> 00:05:20.325
and a charred broccoli chimichurri on top.

00:05:20.325 --> 00:05:22.572
(dramatic music)

00:05:22.572 --> 00:05:25.480
- [Yadi] One for each of you.

00:05:25.480 --> 00:05:27.480
- Ready, okay. Let's go.

00:05:29.818 --> 00:05:31.789
- It's not that strong of a broccoli taste

00:05:31.789 --> 00:05:33.079
at all. There's a lot going on.

00:05:33.079 --> 00:05:33.912
- Yeah.

00:05:36.278 --> 00:05:37.949
- If it were not for the color,

00:05:37.949 --> 00:05:41.621
I wouldn't know that there was
like green veggies in here.

00:05:41.621 --> 00:05:43.719
- I think that slight
edge is going to go to the

00:05:43.719 --> 00:05:47.269
veggie dish. I like the
spicy Jalapenos going on.

00:05:47.269 --> 00:05:48.923
- This is really hard, because like, both

00:05:48.923 --> 00:05:50.413
of them were really
good and they were both

00:05:50.413 --> 00:05:52.237
super flavorful. I
thought it was interesting

00:05:52.237 --> 00:05:54.135
that both dishes also had corn.

00:05:54.135 --> 00:05:56.829
I think the corn masked the
broccoli taste really well.

00:05:56.829 --> 00:05:58.850
But I feel like I prefer the appetizer

00:05:58.850 --> 00:06:00.699
dish over the steak dish.

00:06:00.699 --> 00:06:03.119
- The appetizer dish had so many

00:06:03.119 --> 00:06:05.142
different flavors. And when I was biting

00:06:05.142 --> 00:06:07.372
into it and thinking
about how many vegetables

00:06:07.372 --> 00:06:09.775
were in it, I was just like so shocked.

00:06:09.775 --> 00:06:11.636
And the steak dish was
also great. The fact that

00:06:11.636 --> 00:06:14.509
it had like vegetables and broccoli on it,

00:06:14.509 --> 00:06:17.092
but I liked the appetizer dish.

00:06:18.501 --> 00:06:22.361
- Dare I say, do we have some
broccoli lovers a little bit?

00:06:22.361 --> 00:06:25.410
If it was... did you
love the broccoli today?

00:06:25.410 --> 00:06:28.058
- I'm not a broccoli lover, per say.

00:06:28.058 --> 00:06:30.153
But, I'm a believer now that you can make

00:06:30.153 --> 00:06:32.995
broccoli taste good if you have some

00:06:32.995 --> 00:06:37.008
bomb ass professional
chefs prepare it for you.

00:06:37.008 --> 00:06:39.752
- My mom would be smiling
really proudly right now.

00:06:39.752 --> 00:06:41.290
Maybe crying.

00:06:41.290 --> 00:06:42.904
- Yes!

00:06:42.904 --> 00:06:46.245
- So do you think we
slayed this challenge?

00:06:46.245 --> 00:06:50.078
- Teamwork make the
dreamwork, baby. It's lit.

00:06:59.175 --> 00:07:00.092
- Broccoli!

